## Part B: Deeper analysis from the dataset

These come from analysing the Sales Data sheet. They are not charts on the dashboard.

### Q8. Is the business growing?
| | 2024 | 2025 | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Revenue | $660K | $759K | +15.0% |
| Gross profit | $336K | $386K | +14.9% |
| Orders | 2,891 | 3,309 | +14.5% |
| Gross margin | 51.0% | 50.9% | flat |

**Answer:** Yes. Growth came from more orders, not higher prices or margins.

### Q9. Does discounting hurt profit?
| Discount | Share of order lines | Gross margin |
|---|---|---|
| 0% | 42.1% | 54.5% |
| 5% | 21.2% | 51.5% |
| 10% | 20.1% | 49.2% |
| 15% | 10.8% | 45.8% |
| 20% | 4.6% | 43.1% |
| 25% | 1.2% | 38.3% |

**Answer:** Yes. Every discount step costs margin, and 25% off earns about 16 points less than full price. About 58% of lines carry some discount, though the revenue-weighted average discount is only 6.7%. Orders at 15% or more are about 17% of lines and earn about 45% margin.

### Q10. Why is Team & Club Sales important?
| Channel | Orders | Avg order value | Avg discount | Gross margin |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Web Store | 2,733 | $187 | 5.3% | 51.5% |
| Team & Club Sales | 406 | $886 | 9.9% | 49.3% |
| Specialty Retail | 1,347 | $172 | 5.6% | 52.2% |
| Mobile App | 998 | $179 | 5.8% | 51.1% |
| Marketplace | 716 | $192 | 6.5% | 50.9% |

**Answer:** Team & Club Sales is 6.5% of orders but 25% of revenue, because orders average about 9 units. It also gets the deepest discounts, so its margin is the lowest of the five channels.

### Q11. Which product categories perform best?
| Category | Revenue | Share | Gross margin |
|---|---|---|---|
| Camp & Cook | $403K | 28.4% | 49.8% |
| Snow Sports | $312K | 22.0% | 50.4% |
| Trail Running | $286K | 20.1% | 54.5% |
| Paddle Sports | $260K | 18.3% | 50.1% |
| Climbing | $157K | 11.1% | 49.9% |

**Answer:** Camp & Cook is the largest category, but Trail Running earns the best margin by about 4 points.

### Q12. Which products have the best and worst margins?
| | Product | Gross margin |
|---|---|---|
| Best | Chalk Bag Set | 70% |
| Best | Compression Calf Sleeves | 68% |
| Best | Dry Bag 20L | 68% |
| Worst | Geodesic Tent 3P | 41% |
| Worst | Dynamic Rope 60m | 41% |
| Worst | Avalanche Probe Kit | 41% |

**Answer:** Low-priced accessories earn the highest margins. The Geodesic Tent is a top-five revenue product but one of the lowest-margin items.

### Q13. Which markets earn the lowest margins?
**Answer:** South America has the lowest regional margin at 47%, against 51-53% elsewhere. By country, Argentina (45%), Colombia (48%), Mexico (49%) and Chile (48%) sit below the rest, while New Zealand is highest at 53%.

### Q14. Are there seasonal patterns?
**Answer:** Yes, and they flip by hemisphere. Snow Sports sells in December to February in northern markets (50% of northern snow revenue) but in June to August in southern markets (41% of southern snow revenue). Revenue per day during Black Friday week (24-30 November) is about 1.9x the average day.

### Q15. Who buys: new or repeat customers?
| Customer type | Revenue | Share | Avg order value |
|---|---|---|---|
| Repeat | $606K | 42.7% | $183 |
| Club/Group | $410K | 28.9% | $590 |
| First-time | $402K | 28.3% | $183 |

**Answer:** Repeat customers are the largest group. Club/Group customers are only 11% of orders but 29% of revenue.

